WEBVTT

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.330
mirai michibiku hikari ni nare
So be my guiding light to the future!

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.740
﻿That bald one got ahead of me!

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.790
﻿What is that glow?

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.960
﻿I'll catch it!

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:08.980
﻿Did something fall?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.780
﻿It is by the grace of the universe

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.570
﻿that the land is blessed.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.740
﻿It is because of the sacred taboo

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:07.750
﻿that people can live out their
﻿lives in eternal tranquility.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.790
﻿Open your hearts wide to Heaven.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:15.760
﻿For it is Heaven that bestows upon us
﻿the source of life and sustenance.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.630
﻿- Go over there.
- ﻿Sorry.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.870
﻿- Why did you dodge?
- ﻿Yes.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.410
﻿You taught us that we must always respond
﻿dynamically to the situation, Captain.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.460
﻿What are you smiling for?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.460
﻿Bell skipped two grades.
﻿I'd expect no less from him.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.090
﻿Inspect and equip your backpacks!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.470
﻿Hey, there.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.640
﻿Congratulations!

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.890
﻿First practical space training!

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.940
﻿Manny came too!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.020
﻿Hey.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.230
﻿Is that a HAROBE?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.480
﻿Hurray! Hurray!

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.530
﻿Bellri.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:01.110
﻿Luin, you do your best too.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:01.780
﻿I will.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.910
﻿St. Flower Academy girls, get out!

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.240
﻿- Come on, girls!
- ﻿Bell, do your best in training!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.040
﻿Go for it! Go for it!

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.710
﻿Catch those girls!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.380
﻿Instructor, they're just here to cheer us on?

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.210
﻿Even you, our best student, is saying that?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.380
﻿Have some consideration for
﻿the guys without girlfriends.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.640
﻿Even if you're the Operations Director's kid

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.640
﻿that doesn't give you any right to
﻿drag girls from Kuntala aboard.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.640
﻿I didn't call them here.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:37.020
﻿Hurray! Hurray! Hurray! 1010th class!

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.150
﻿Run for the Crown's operating room!

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.900
﻿- Everyone!
﻿- Capital Guard!

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.030
﻿Those cheerleaders have
﻿run in your direction.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.030
﻿Huh? Roger that.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.870
﻿Everyone, back to your seats.
﻿Check your equipment.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.040
﻿Head back and check your
﻿life support equipment!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.500
﻿Air and water pellets, check!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.420
﻿Check!

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.300
﻿MMF functioning properly!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.420
﻿There's a lot of Sprites today...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.300
﻿Sprites?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.180
﻿You're not a student, are you?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.760
﻿Who are you?

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.560
﻿Raraiya Monday.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.270
﻿Not again.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.400
﻿You know you're not allowed to cheer
﻿them on during practical training!

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:23.030
﻿This girl is under the surveillance
﻿of the Capital Army.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:24.450
﻿Capital Army?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.530
﻿Surveillance? What's with that?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.370
﻿Don't ask! Kuntala!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.990
﻿- You kicked her!
- It's the Under Nut.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.330
﻿Passing through Under Nut.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.590
﻿The nut we just passed through
﻿is the Under Nut.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:48.930
﻿This poor nut is not counted among
﻿the 144 nuts in Capital Tower.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.510
﻿Does anyone know the reason?

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.680
- ﻿Torriti.
- ﻿Sir.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.310
﻿Prior to the construction of Capital Tower,

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:58.480
﻿it was an artificial satellite built to
﻿clear space debris from the UC era.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:05.780
Even in low orbit, the cables and nuts move
﻿in sync with Earth's rotation. Why is that?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.530
﻿- Hey!
﻿- Huh?

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.240
﻿Were you not listening?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.450
﻿It's such a boring question...

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.830
﻿Not again.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.080
﻿Regurgitate the textbook
﻿if you want, just answer!

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:20.460
﻿Because of the Minovsky Magnet-ray Field,

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.750
﻿or MMF, effect produced
﻿between the cables and nuts.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.380
﻿- In particular...
- ﻿That's enough.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.550
﻿What is the source of that energy?

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.050
﻿You already know the answer.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.300
﻿- Tell me.
﻿- The Earth's...

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:36.520
﻿upper atmosphere contains an Airglow Belt,
﻿which generates energy that the cable absorbs.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.690
﻿That's correct. What's our present altitude?
﻿Luin Lee!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.480
﻿365 kilometers.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:47.490
﻿Dynamic vision is a vital weapon
﻿when working in space!

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:51.950
﻿Because radar is useless once
﻿Minovsky Particles are spread around!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.120
﻿Yes, sir!

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.790
Gloves on! Helmets in hand!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.160
﻿Don't cry!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.050
- Is this HAROBE yours?
- Yes.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.550
There's no need for a Kuntala
﻿to have one, is there?

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:09.510
﻿A HAROBE for environmental
﻿testing is a necessity.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.840
﻿She's called Nobell.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:14.970
﻿Now listen here! You've got to stop this
﻿future husband search of yours already.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.930
﻿It's a tradition at Saint Flower Academy.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:21.900
﻿We've been saving to buy these tickets
﻿since we entered the academy.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.860
﻿What is the Capital Army?

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:27.030
﻿Is it different from the Capital Guard?

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.950
﻿We're arriving at the First Nut.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.990
﻿Come on, you're getting off here, right?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.580
﻿Our tickets are good until the next nut.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.580
﻿- This way.
- ﻿Right.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.850
﻿After I went to the trouble of
﻿catching her in midair...

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.060
﻿She doesn't seem to feel a thing.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.230
﻿She's from Ameria or Gondwan.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:05.310
﻿She can't be from Towasanga, right?

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.020
﻿Who cares?

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:11.280
﻿I've never seen the type of Mobile
﻿Suit she came down in before.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.030
﻿Treat her well.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.700
﻿Why can't we cheer for them?

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.290
﻿Because it's a nuisance.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.080
﻿What's with that girl?

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:27.090
﻿Pressurizing for Minovsky Flight.
﻿One, two, three. Good.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.550
﻿MMF Position, good. Route is clear.

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:34.930
﻿You jumped down from ridiculously high,

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.140
﻿so the oxygen deprivation
﻿was harsh, is that it?

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.310
﻿The Captain was the one to save her,
so it's little wonder he's taken an interest.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:55.240
﻿Fight! Fight!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.620
﻿Okay! All groups, board Rectens!

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.830
﻿Once you have boarded and
﻿made your first movement,

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.670
﻿switch places with the next student.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:05.790
﻿Why me?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.500
﻿It's in order of age,
﻿so you're first, right, Bell?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.550
﻿Ah! Right!

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.230
﻿No way.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.160
﻿Why is the cockpit facing outside?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.160
﻿Practical training is a form of student
﻿hazing. What can you do?

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.920
﻿This is training to teach the skills
needed to live in space.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:47.750
﻿Yes, sir!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.340
﻿Hurry up and board,
﻿then make your first movement.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:51.460
﻿Yes, sir!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.350
﻿Those guys...

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.360
﻿For my first movement.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:10.810
﻿Bellri, you're slow.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.780
﻿Right. Raise both arms and move.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.200
﻿Test the full movement of both arms...

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.910
﻿Minovsky Particles, you say?

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.840
﻿Those aren't Capital Guard machines...

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.920
﻿Pirates! Once Minovsky Particles are spread,

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.670
﻿we can only use wired communications.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:40.140
﻿Pirates? The rumored space pirates?

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.430
﻿That's not a Recten's silhouette.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:48.060
﻿What? It's coming this way?

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.110
﻿- Nice!
- ﻿Just one machine?!

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:56.490
﻿That's not a pirate Mobile Suit!

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:57.990
﻿What?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.510
﻿Students aboard the Rectens, don't move!

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:18.920
﻿Let them think they're unmanned.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.510
﻿It's aiming its rifle at us!

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.840
﻿Connect.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:23.260
﻿G! G!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.510
﻿- G!
- What did she say?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.280
G...

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.270
﻿Don't use a contact link either.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.440
﻿- Cut your power.
- ﻿But then—

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.020
﻿- Then—
﻿- Cut your camera.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.690
﻿- Come on—
- ﻿A murderer like you—

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:41.160
﻿If I can't move, what's the point
﻿of having a Mobile Suit?

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.290
﻿Who's that girl sitting in the seat?

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:49.620
﻿I have taken this Crown hostage.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.120
﻿I will release it in 20 minutes.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:56.380
﻿I permit you to communicate that
﻿information to Capital Tower.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.170
﻿And if we don't listen to you, then what?!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.880
﻿Use your imagination.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.680
﻿I won't sever the cable or
﻿anything like that.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.940
﻿Is she not here?

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:22.740
﻿There she is! Is that okay?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:28.040
﻿A welder is similar to a beam rifle.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:31.710
﻿There's gunpowder for operating
﻿it in an emergency.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.460
﻿I should be able to advance or
﻿withdraw two or three times.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.690
﻿Torriti's Recten got taken out!

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.020
﻿Bridge! Check!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.400
﻿- It caught us again!
- ﻿It's coming up!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.240
﻿That's not Torriti.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:05.200
﻿This girl is responding to it.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.910
﻿Have her memories returned?

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:09.620
﻿Hey! Raraiya Monday, right?

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.660
﻿Raraiya?

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.370
﻿These levers are for the Big Arms.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.130
﻿Each has three charges of gunpowder
﻿for emergency operation.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:20.590
﻿I don't know what kind of firepower they have.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.630
﻿Or that!

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.520
﻿If she wants a fight...!

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.820
﻿Stop being a pirate!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:51.160
﻿I won't let you shoot!

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.870
﻿Wh-What? This Recten's Big Arm...

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.790
﻿He can't damage the cable...
﻿Where is he?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.420
﻿Even if you use the cable as a shield...!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.470
﻿The position the enemy would never expect

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.100
﻿will become the most advantageous
position for me!

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.270
How will I do this without damaging
the Crown or cable?

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.480
﻿Like this?

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.440
﻿The world...

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.650
...﻿is not square!

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.410
﻿Like this, then this right?

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.170
﻿I'll melt your face off with this welder!

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.710
﻿Surrender!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.840
﻿Why are you resorting to piracy?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.470
﻿What's wrong, G-Self?
﻿That's not the right response.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:50.140
﻿Whose Recten is that?

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.350
﻿It's Bell's, don't you think?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.970
- ﻿He's being too reckless!
- G!

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.560
﻿Everyone, put on space suits.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.810
﻿There's no telling when we might
﻿be thrown out into the void!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.770
﻿Dellensen, heading out.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:05.990
﻿Who are you?

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.070
﻿Luin Lee. From behind you.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.740
﻿Equipping Big Arm and Power Weld.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.450
﻿The Crown that descended has
﻿been occupied by pirates.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.490
﻿You get that, right?

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.120
﻿Go back to the Crown!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.370
﻿If you leave the MMF Field,
﻿you'll be pulled down by the Earth.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.340
﻿That won't happen to this unit!

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.670
﻿Accelerate!

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:36.890
﻿What about the Crown that descended?!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.980
﻿I know, but...

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.940
﻿If we get a little scared
﻿because of a battery thief,

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:42.270
﻿this will keep happening forever.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:47.150
﻿Hey, now. This is your first time doing
﻿practical training in space, right?

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.450
﻿I've done the simulations before.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.200
﻿This welder can become a beam rifle.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.660
﻿I know that little trick.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:58.410
﻿That's the same model as the
﻿one that dropped Raraiya.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.080
﻿Who's Raraiya?

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.260
﻿I'll use the Beam Saber.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:12.720
﻿What?

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.220
﻿The SU-Cord!

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.120
﻿There's explosives set in our backpacks.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.500
﻿you resist, we will destroy your engine.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.420
﻿You hear me, woman?

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.920
﻿What?

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.840
﻿Bellri. Do you read me?

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.510
I do.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.130
﻿Is that you, Luin?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.880
﻿Cut that out! Stop it!

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.050
﻿- G!
﻿- What are you doing?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.390
﻿What's with this girl?

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:58.640
﻿She's a prisoner. A prisoner captured
﻿by Captain Dellensen.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.100
﻿So she's the girl who the
﻿Capital Army brought from space?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.100
﻿I don't know anything about that.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:06.860
﻿Are you?

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:08.040
﻿G...

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.860
﻿This girl's in bad shape.

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:12.050
﻿G...

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.300
﻿What's going on?

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.510
﻿Is that the pirate?

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:33.380
﻿It's here! It's here!

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.630
﻿This girl...

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:47.690
<i>﻿Time-wise. Cahill's unit which occupied
﻿the descending Crown</i>

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.820
<i>﻿should have retrieved the
﻿Photon Battery by now.</i>

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:54.190
<i>﻿But because I get like this sometimes...</i>

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.160
﻿Please move to the Crown.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.410
﻿Your hatch conforms to
﻿international standards, right?

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.910
﻿Don't act so familiar!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.370
﻿Did you say something?

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:03.200
﻿No.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:10.210
﻿There was something wrong
﻿with this unit today.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.380
﻿Bell returns alive!

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.840
﻿Hey, thank you.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.180
﻿Good work.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:22.010
﻿The cockpit is on the upper floor.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.100
﻿Right.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:29.350
- Bell!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.110
﻿G!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.860
﻿G's...

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.860
﻿Stop it!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.990
﻿She came alone, without any support,

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:45.160
﻿You were planning to withdraw from here
﻿five minutes after the guys who went below.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.710
﻿If your Rectens hadn't gotten in the way...

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:50.130
﻿Don't give me that self-serving nonsense!

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:53.130
﻿You knock around my precious
﻿student, Torriti, and—

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.260
﻿My aim is precise.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.840
﻿I did not cause his unit to explode.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:02.390
﻿A competent pilot would be able to
﻿return to the Crown on his own.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:04.720
﻿What?

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.310
﻿She's not cute at all.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.600
﻿State your name and rank
﻿in the Amerian military.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.320
﻿I am not a member of the military.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.730
﻿Only the military uses Mobile Suits.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.070
﻿What's your name and rank?

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.950
﻿Aida Rayhunton. Space Pirate.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.200
﻿You just stole two names
﻿and stuck them together!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:31.290
﻿Your unit is the one that came down
﻿here a week ago, isn't it?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.040
﻿I invoke the right to refuse.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.340
﻿A pirate's in no position to
﻿demand any rights!

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.300
﻿It's because of feelings like yours
﻿that people kill each other.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:42.590
﻿Instructor.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:46.310
﻿This pilot has shut her hatch.
﻿It won't open.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.850
﻿G-Self.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:51.310
﻿That unit's hatch can't be
﻿opened by anyone but me.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.190
﻿Thankee.

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.650
﻿Not at all.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:08.790
Luin.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:08.810
﻿- No way!
- Don't you move.
Luin.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:11.920
﻿- No way!
- Don't you move.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:13.630
﻿G is...!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.960
﻿Ah! No!

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.710
﻿Come on, you're all right now.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.800
﻿Maybe this girl and that unit...

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.630
- Yeah, there's some connection between them.
- ﻿G!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.260
﻿It's practically brand new.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.680
﻿Looks like it.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:27.680
﻿- Pipe down!
- Mr. Army Man!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.680
﻿Let that girl rest.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.690
﻿- Please, do!
- ﻿Come along, young lady!

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.150
﻿Rayhunton Code.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.900
﻿These all conform to international standards.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.190
﻿Confirmed.

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:40.110
﻿What?

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:42.900
﻿There's some meaning to this.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.580
﻿Since the same pattern showed up
﻿on the monitor. In that case...

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.870
